# Proxion Messenger environment template
# Copy to .env and adjust. Every value is optional: with no .env at all the
# gateway serves https://127.0.0.1:8080 (self-signed cert) with no pod backing.
# (.env is gitignored, so this template is safe to commit.)
# Every variable is listed in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# ─── Network ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROXION_HTTP_PORT=8080
# PROXION_WS_PORT=7474
# Interface to bind. 127.0.0.1 keeps the gateway local-only.
# PROXION_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Public URLs advertised to browsers and federation peers. Required when
# running behind a reverse proxy (Caddy, nginx) or exposing the gateway to
# the internet; leave unset for local use.
# PROXION_PUBLIC_URL=wss://chat.example.com/ws
# PROXION_HTTP_PUBLIC_URL=https://chat.example.com
# PROXION_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://chat.example.com

# TLS. With no cert set, run_gateway.py makes a self-signed one in
# <data dir>/tls. Set PROXION_AUTO_TLS=0 for plain http/ws (behind a reverse
# proxy that terminates TLS, or loopback-only use).
# PROXION_AUTO_TLS=1
# PROXION_SSL_CERT=/certs/fullchain.pem
# PROXION_SSL_KEY=/certs/privkey.pem

# ─── Storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where identity keys and the local message store live.
# Default: ./data next to run_gateway.py (~/.proxion/data for a packaged
# executable). The desktop app sets its own.
# PROXION_DATA_DIR=

# ─── Solid Pod (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pod sign-in normally happens in the browser via Solid OIDC, so no credentials
# belong here. Set these ONLY for a headless gateway with its own account on a
# CSS, JSS or NSS server (the URL selects the server type):
# PROXION_CSS_URL=
# PROXION_CSS_EMAIL=
# PROXION_CSS_PASSWORD=

# ─── Voice/video relay (TURN) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Calls connect peer-to-peer. When both sides are on ordinary home networks a
# direct path is usually found using STUN alone (built in, no config). On a
# restrictive network (symmetric NAT, or a corporate/mobile firewall) there is
# no direct path and the call needs a TURN relay to get through. The web client
# falls back to the free public relay openrelay.metered.ca unless the user turns
# it off in Settings > Calls. Point these at your own coturn and the gateway
# hands clients short-lived credentials for it. See docs/CALLS.md and
# docs/SELF_HOSTING.md.
# TURN_URL=turn:relay.example.com:3478
# TURN_SECRET=

# ─── Federation safety ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Allow relaying to localhost/LAN gateways. Only enable for local two-gateway
# development (see scripts/run_local_pair.py); keep 0 on anything internet-facing.
PROXION_ALLOW_PRIVATE_RELAY=0

# Solid access grants (delegated third-party pod access). Off by default;
# enable only if your deployment profile requires third-party data sharing.
PROXION_ENABLE_ACCESS_GRANTS=0

# ─── Advanced ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hardening, Solid SDK migration stages, relay fallback, and every other knob
# are documented in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
